WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.930
What Webb saw in the Tarantula.

00:02.726 --> 00:06.855
Seen from our side, this cloud's light is the Webb telescope's own picture.

00:07.328 --> 00:12.505
It is made in infrared light, which no eye can see, so every colour in it is chosen.

00:13.017 --> 00:19.747
Infrared passes through dust, and here it shows tens of thousands of young stars that no telescope had seen.

00:20.307 --> 00:25.763
The region is 340 light-years across, in a small galaxy beside ours.
